  "subgroup_and_bypassed_work": "One independent single-entry family; each strategy selects solely from numeric entries (conditional unique sign/zero subgroups), bypassing subscript interpretation and row-column lookup. Keys/solutions are used only for independent scoring.",
  "construction_proof": "code = uniform random sample of 4*n^4 complete instances. code%4 chooses one of four positions; remaining radix digits choose each cell from the identical integer set. The target position is independent of all numeric entries. Thus unique sign, zero, value rank or magnitude is not assigned to the correct location; every fixed matrix is compatible with all four targets. No option-bank or layout annotation exists. Repeated/constant values are legitimate lookup collapses, not rejected.",
  "limits": "72 independent ordinary records on seeds 71 and 991 are bounded probes. Conditional small-subgroup perfect results do not establish a recurring cue. No balancing quotas or excluded valid cases result from scores. All-equal matrices naturally permit value copying; detecting a distinct location is then unobservable in an integer-only response.",
  "short_batch": "Requested seed 60419 is unchanged; all three delivered lookups within each band have distinct (target,value). Repeated target positions in moderate/hard do not bypass numeric lookup; no coverage quota applies to three-record batches.",
  "learner_selection": "Inspected engine/rust/question_selection.rs:125-198. It selects by eligible IDs/difficulty, configured weights and hashed seed, not matrix values or target positions. Live history filtering/weights are inaccessible and untested in this offline job; publication audit captured basis 1 is distinct from learner selection.",
